# Maslosoft Signals

Signals connects PHP application components through generated annotation metadata.
Use `emit()` to send a cloned message to each registered receiver, or `gather()` to
instantiate providers registered for a discovery slot.

Requires **PHP 8.5 or newer**, EmbeDi 3.0.1 or newer, and Maslosoft Light 2.

```shell
composer require maslosoft/signals
```

Make participating classes Composer-autoloadable, configure their source paths in
`signals.yml`, and build the connection definition:

```yaml
paths:
  - src
io:
  class: Maslosoft\Signals\Builder\IO\PhpFile
  generatedPath: generated
```

```shell
composer dump-autoload
vendor/bin/signals build
```

After loading Composer's autoloader, obtain a dispatcher in the current execution
context and dispatch your application's message:

```php
use Maslosoft\Signals\Signal;

$messages = Signal::fly()->emit(new App\Messages\MenuItems());
```

Receivers implement Addendum's `AnnotatedInterface` and declare
`@SlotFor(\App\Messages\MenuItems)` on a class, public method, or public property.
The [emission guide](docs/emit/index.md.php) contains complete message and receiver
examples. [Gathering](docs/gather/index.md.php) uses `@SignalFor` to discover providers.

Definitions and overlays belong to individual dispatcher objects.
`Signal::fly()` deliberately reuses a dispatcher within the current Light context.
Sequential workers must end that lifetime explicitly; see
[application servers](docs/application-servers/index.md.php).

Read [configuration](docs/configuration/index.md.php),
[generation and deployment](docs/generate/index.md.php),
[filters](docs/filters/index.md.php), and
[migration](docs/migration/index.md.php) for details.

For development:

```shell
composer install
composer check
```

